{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794391105,"nonce":"dk8srUMbFuaT1vKUzPFfpxGHXMc=","title":"GPU animation P0: baseline measurements, one frame clock, and the groundwork the later phases need","message":"Part of the GPU-deferral plan (umbrella issue). No behaviour change in this phase.\n\n**Measure first.** Nothing in the plan is justified without numbers, and none exist yet. Build a small set of scenes and record CPU and GPU time per frame for each, split by stage (scheduler tick, tree walk, element collection, patch, upload bytes, encode, GPU pass time):\n- 200 cards animating transform and opacity through CSS transitions;\n- a long list scrolling, and a fling;\n- three spinners on an otherwise idle window;\n- a live window resize;\n- the russl toy preview with a flow shader (see 59d424e).\nRecord medians as a comment on this issue. iPhone numbers use the method in 36c7812 (xctrace Metal System Trace); the Linux box's software adapters are not valid for GPU timing.\n\n**One frame clock.** Today there are at least six time bases: the scheduler (Instant, EMA-smoothed, 32 ms cap), motions (integer ms, clamped to 1..50), CSS animations and FLIP (integer ms, 50 ms cap), scroll physics (microseconds, 100 ms cap), AnimatedKeyframe delay (wall clock), flow shaders (app_clock_secs). Add one monotonic `FrameClock` in blinc_core, set once per frame and readable from every consumer. New code uses it; the old integrators stay until their phase.\n\n**A time field in the SDF uniforms.** `Uniforms` carries only `viewport_size`. Add `time` (and keep the struct 16-byte aligned), uploaded once per frame. `GlassUniforms.time` is declared and uploaded but no shader reads it, and `GpuRenderer::update_time` has no callers: wire it to the clock or delete it.\n\n**Node slot lane (spike).** `GpuPrimitive` is 34 vec4 (544 B), with no node id, no opacity and no time. P2 needs a `node_slot` per primitive. Decide between a spare u32 lane and a new vec4 (+16 B, one more data-texture row). Check first that `type_info[3]` is not overloaded: Mesh primitives reuse it as a per-vertex-colour flag. List every place a field must be added: the Rust struct, russl `Primitive`, the tier-2 loader in `access.rs`, the tier-1 `SdfVertexInstance` attributes and each `vs_main`, `tests/primitive_layout.rs`, and about fifteen full struct literals (`paint/rects.rs`, `shadows.rs`, `circles.rs`, `from_glyph`, ...). `GpuGlyph` (96 B) needs the same lane for moving text.\n\n**Semver preparation.** None of RenderProps, KeyframeProperties, MotionBindings or ElementStyle is `#[non_exhaustive]`, so any new field breaks exhaustive literals. Add the attribute to the animation-facing structs once, in the 0.7.0 breaking release, and list the breakages in the repo and in the sibling blinc_abi repo.\n\n**Small fixes found on the way.** `RendererConfig` says 20,000 primitives is about 400 KB; at 544 B it is about 10.9 MB. `crates/blinc_animation/README.md` documents methods that do not exist (`Spring::animate_to`, `update`, `SpringConfig::bouncy`).\n\nAcceptance: baseline recorded; clock and uniform in place with the old paths untouched; node-slot decision and the list of edit sites written up here.","files":null}]}